{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7d1c2f4-5a3e-4c9b-9f21-7e6a0d3c8b15",
    "name": "Blog API - Node.js + Express (Task 2)",
    "description": "Complete Postman collection for the MERN blog platform REST API (Task 2).\n\n## How to use\n1. Start the backend: `cd backend` then `npm run dev`\n2. Confirm the server is on http://localhost:5000 (change the `baseUrl` collection variable if needed)\n3. Run a folder with the Collection Runner, or send requests one by one\n\n## Folders\n- **Health Check** - quick server status\n- **Posts** - GET all (paginated), GET by id, POST, PUT, DELETE\n- **Comments** - GET comments of a post, POST comment, DELETE comment\n- **Error Cases** - 400 validation errors, 404 missing resources, unknown routes, malformed JSON\n\n## Notes\n- Data is stored **in memory**: restarting the server resets everything to the seed data.\n- Routes work both with and without the `/api` prefix (e.g. `/posts` and `/api/posts`).\n- `createdPostId` / `createdCommentId` are filled in automatically by the create requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health Check",
      "description": "Verifies that the API process is running.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET Health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Body reports success', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(json.message).to.include('running');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the API status, environment and current timestamp."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
